# house-pause-options — open the PAUSE menu (ESC), navigate to OPTIONS
# (entry type 2), press Z (A=0x10) to open the type-2 options submenu, then
# (rebased on OPTIONS_READY) drive the config-panel nav: move the cursor down
# through all five rows and change three values — Sound (numeric +1), Message
# Speed (SLOW→MED, a word), Unread Text Skip (OFF→ON, a word).  Exercises the
# render FUN_0049c050 at every selected row + the numeric AND word value paths.
#
# Engine: FUN_0047fc44 update / FUN_0048150c→FUN_0049c050 render, dispatched
# from FUN_0047fa76 / FUN_004820ba at sub_anim==10 / sub_anim>0.  Derived from
# house-pause-encyclopedia-nav (load fa7c82 → HOUSE idle, {phasepin 80}).
#
# Nav: the house pause list is [1,6,2,3,4] = Items·Encyclopedia·Options·Save·Exit,
# default selection index 0 (Items).  Options is index 2 ⇒ TWO downs to open.
#
# Sync: the menu OPEN rebases on PAUSE_READY (pause-load-done edge); the config
# nav rebases on OPTIONS_READY — the rising edge of "Options submenu navigable"
# (scene 9, sub_anim==10, Options selected).  OPTIONS_READY fires AFTER PAUSE_OPEN
# on both sides, so the v3 identity join keys to it consistently (PAUSE_READY is
# STRADDLED by PAUSE_OPEN — pre-load on the port, post-load on retail — which
# mispairs the window).  Drive with `--anchor OPTIONS_READY`.
